{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'jq . docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/artifacts/epic/001-epic-review.json'","aggregated_output":"{\n  \"command\": \"epic-review\",\n  \"version\": 1,\n  \"status\": \"blocked\",\n  \"outcome\": \"block\",\n  \"result\": {\n    \"outcome\": \"block\",\n    \"canonicalReview\": {\n      \"outcome\": \"block\",\n      \"reviewerLabels\": [\n        \"epic-reviewer-1\",\n        \"epic-reviewer-2\"\n      ],\n      \"reconciliationSummary\": \"Both reviewer blockers remain supported by current code and epic evidence. Reviewer 1's over-large tool-result recovery blocker is confirmed because intake/queued handling applies the large-tier truncation rule, while turn-close recovery independently calls summarizeToolResult without the tier gate or summary parameters. Reviewer 2's absent-derivation fallback logging blocker is confirmed because compose records a dependency gap for missing rows but only emits a recovery receipt when a row exists, and derive logs only recovery receipts. The duplicate rename findings are merged as one nonblocking finding. Gates were rerun locally and passed, with real-inference tests skipped because LHC_OPENROUTER_KEY is unset.\",\n      \"crossStoryFindings\": [\n        \"Flows 2 and 3 diverge at consumption-time recovery: the queued tool-result path satisfies over-large tool_result_summary derivations by deterministic truncation, but turn-close recovery reimplements tool-result recovery and can invoke inference for the same tier.\",\n        \"Flow 3 and Flow 5 diverge for absent derivation rows: composition marks a fallback/gap, but the logging path only logs recoveries for existing rows.\",\n        \"No material fake adapter, hidden shim, placeholder provider, or non-real default production path was verified under packages/lhc/src; deterministic providers remain explicit test/config fixtures.\"\n      ],\n      \"architectureFindings\": [\n        \"Tech-design DD-3 requires tool results above the large tier to land ready by deterministic truncation with no inference item/provider call; packages/lhc/src/domains/messages/index.ts:150-196 and packages/lhc/src/domains/messages/internal/handlers.ts:145-159 implement that for intake/queued work, but packages/lhc/src/domains/turns/internal/derive.ts:117-127 bypasses it during recovery.\",\n        \"Tech-design DD-5 and epic AC-3.6/AC-5.3 require fallback events to be logged separately from derivation state; packages/lhc/src/domains/turns/internal/compose.ts:222-238 omits a RecoveryReceipt when the derivation row is absent, so packages/lhc/src/domains/turns/internal/derive.ts:196-211 has nothing to log.\",\n        \"The form-to-derivation rename is incomplete at the production vocabulary level: schema/shared types are renamed, but production modules still expose form-named files, helpers, constants, and comments.\"\n      ],\n      \"epicCoverageAssessment\": [\n        \"Story Gate passed locally: cd packages/lhc && pnpm run verify completed with 47 test files passed, 426 tests passed, and 9 skipped.\",\n        \"Epic Gate passed locally: cd packages/lhc && pnpm run verify-all completed with 47 test files passed, 426 tests passed, and 9 skipped.\",\n        \"Coverage remains incomplete for cross-story recovery: tests cover over-large tool results on intake/queued handling and normal composition fallback, but not failed/pending over-large tool_result_summary recovery at turn close.\",\n        \"Coverage remains incomplete for absent derivation-row fallback logging: tests cover pending/failed row fallback logging, but not missing-row fallback logging.\",\n        \"Flow 5/6 logging and runtime-change coverage is otherwise present; Flow 0 rename coverage is partial because stale production vocabulary remains.\"\n      ],\n      \"productionPathFindings\": [\n        \"packages/lhc/src/domains/turns/internal/derive.ts:117-127 performs a real provider call for tool_result_summary recovery with raw content, unknown_tool, no targetTokens, and no guidance. For over-large tool results this violates the deterministic truncation/no-inference production invariant.\",\n        \"packages/lhc/src/domains/turns/internal/compose.ts:148-153 correctly defines the tool-result fallback as truncateForFallback, but recoverMessageForms runs before composition and can replace a non-ready row with provider output, preventing the deterministic floor path from being used for over-large sources.\",\n        \"Smart compact was not found to call a provider in the inspected production path; compact resolves chunk material through the turns surface and stored-member concatenation.\"\n      ],\n      \"blockingFindings\": [\n        {\n          \"id\": \"E06-BLOCK-001\",\n          \"severity\": \"major\",\n          \"title\": \"Turn-close recovery bypasses the tool-result large-tier gate\",\n          \"evidence\": \"The queued handler returns truncateForFallback(content) as ready with no provider call when estimateTokens(content) exceeds largeTierTokens at packages/lhc/src/domains/messages/internal/handlers.ts:145-159; intake also writes the large summary ready and avoids queueing at packages/lhc/src/domains/messages/index.ts:150-196. Turn-close recovery separately calls run.provider.summarizeToolResult for tool_result_summary at packages/lhc/src/domains/turns/internal/derive.ts:117-127 with raw content, toolName unknown_tool, no targetTokens, and no guidance. This violates AC-2.3, AC-2.7, AC-3.3, and DD-3 for over-large tool results.\",\n          \"affectedFiles\": [\n            \"packages/lhc/src/domains/turns/internal/derive.ts\",\n            \"packages/lhc/src/domains/messages/internal/handlers.ts\",\n            \"packages/lhc/src/domains/messages/index.ts\"\n          ],\n          \"requirementIds\": [\n            \"AC-2.3\",\n            \"AC-2.4\",\n            \"AC-2.7\",\n            \"AC-3.3\",\n            \"DD-3\"\n          ],\n          \"recommendedFixScope\": \"quick-fix\",\n          \"blocking\": true\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"E06-BLOCK-002\",\n          \"severity\": \"major\",\n          \"title\": \"Absent derivation fallback is not logged\",\n          \"evidence\": \"packages/lhc/src/domains/turns/internal/compose.ts:222-238 creates a DependencyGap whenever a derivable component falls back, but creates a RecoveryReceipt only when form !== undefined. packages/lhc/src/domains/turns/internal/derive.ts:196-211 logs only recoveries. Therefore an absent smoothed_prompt or tool_result_summary row can render through fallback and record a gap without producing the fallback log entry required by AC-3.6 and AC-5.3.\",\n          \"affectedFiles\": [\n            \"packages/lhc/src/domains/turns/internal/compose.ts\",\n            \"packages/lhc/src/domains/turns/internal/derive.ts\"\n          ],\n          \"requirementIds\": [\n            \"AC-3.6\",\n            \"AC-5.3\"\n          ],\n          \"recommendedFixScope\": \"quick-fix\",\n          \"blocking\": true\n        }\n      ],\n      \"nonBlockingFindings\": [\n        {\n          \"id\": \"E06-NB-001\",\n          \"severity\": \"major\",\n          \"title\": \"Form-to-derivation rename remains incomplete in production vocabulary\",\n          \"evidence\": \"The epic scope and DD-1 require a total form-to-derivation rename. Current production source still contains form-named APIs and constants, including ComposeFormRow and composeFormKey in packages/lhc/src/domains/turns/internal/compose.ts:38-49, MESSAGE_WORK_FORMS in packages/lhc/src/domains/messages/index.ts:135-140, readMessageFormRows in packages/lhc/src/domains/turns/internal/forms.ts:76-108, readOwnedForms in packages/lhc/src/domains/turns/internal/forms.ts:181+, and imports/usages in packages/lhc/src/domains/turns/index.ts:34-37.\",\n          \"affectedFiles\": [\n            \"packages/lhc/src/domains/turns/internal/compose.ts\",\n            \"packages/lhc/src/domains/messages/index.ts\",\n            \"packages/lhc/src/domains/messages/internal/forms.ts\",\n            \"packages/lhc/src/domains/turns/internal/forms.ts\",\n            \"packages/lhc/src/domains/turns/index.ts\"\n          ],\n          \"requirementIds\": [\n            \"Epic Scope: form-to-derivation rename\",\n            \"Story-0\",\n            \"DD-1\"\n          ],\n          \"recommendedFixScope\": \"fresh-fix-path\",\n          \"blocking\": false\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"E06-NB-002\",\n          \"severity\": \"observation\",\n          \"title\": \"Real-inference tests did not run in the gate environment\",\n          \"evidence\": \"Both local gate runs exited 0, but test output reported NOT-RAN: real-inference (LHC_OPENROUTER_KEY unset) and 9 skipped tests.\",\n          \"affectedFiles\": [\n            \"packages/lhc/test/inference-real.test.ts\"\n          ],\n          \"requirementIds\": [\n            \"Gate Instructions\"\n          ],\n          \"recommendedFixScope\": \"human-ruling\",\n          \"blocking\": false\n        }\n      ],\n      \"unresolvedItems\": [\n        \"Real-inference tests remain skipped in this environment because LHC_OPENROUTER_KEY is unset.\"\n      ],\n      \"gateResult\": \"pass\"\n    },\n    \"verifierResults\": [\n      {\n        \"resultId\": \"319071c1-a8b0-4afc-9a52-ee0b1a424d60\",\n        \"outcome\": \"block\",\n        \"provider\": \"codex\",\n        \"model\": \"gpt-5.5\",\n        \"reviewerLabel\": \"epic-reviewer-1\",\n        \"crossStoryFindings\": [\n          \"Flows 1, 2, and 3 drift at the recovery boundary: queued tool-result derivation applies the large-tier truncation gate, target tokens, paired tool name, and guidance, but turn-close recovery reimplements tool-result recovery separately and omits those Story 2 rules.\",\n          \"No material fake adapter, shim, placeholder, or not-implemented production path was found under packages/lhc/src; deterministic providers remain explicit provider seams and test/config fixtures.\"\n        ],\n        \"architectureFindings\": [\n          \"The tech-design contract DD-3 says over-large tool results are satisfied by deterministic truncation with no inference item/provider call; packages/lhc/src/domains/messages/index.ts:150-196 implements that intake/queue path, but packages/lhc/src/domains/turns/internal/derive.ts:117-127 bypasses it during consumption-time recovery.\",\n          \"The rename is not complete at the code vocabulary level: production modules still expose forms-named files/functions/comments such as packages/lhc/src/domains/messages/internal/forms.ts, packages/lhc/src/domains/turns/internal/forms.ts, readMessageFormRows, readOwnedForms, and numerous src comments using form/form row. Schema and exported shared types are renamed, but the epic requested a codebase-wide form-to-derivation rename.\"\n        ],\n        \"epicCoverageAssessment\": [\n          \"The requested gates passed: pnpm run verify and pnpm run verify-all both completed successfully in packages/lhc.\",\n          \"Coverage is materially incomplete around cross-story recovery: tests cover over-large tool results on intake and normal fallback truncation in composition, but not a failed/pending over-large tool_result_summary with no live work item entering turn-close recovery.\",\n          \"The mapped Flow 5/6 coverage is present for logging and typed runtime-change blocks. Flow 0 rename coverage is only partial because stale production vocabulary remains outside the public shared types/schema.\"\n        ],\n        \"productionPathFindings\": [\n          \"packages/lhc/src/domains/turns/internal/derive.ts:117-127 performs a real provider call for tool_result_summary recovery with raw content, unknown_tool, no targetTokens, and no guidance. For over-large tool results this creates a production execution path that the epic explicitly forbids; the real path should use deterministic truncation and never invoke inference for that tier.\",\n          \"packages/lhc/src/domains/turns/internal/compose.ts:148-153 correctly defines the fallback floor as truncateForFallback, but recoverMessageForms runs before composition and can replace the non-ready row with provider output, preventing the floor path from being used for the same over-large source.\"\n        ],\n        \"blockingFindings\": [\n          {\n            \"id\": \"E06-BLOCK-001\",\n            \"severity\": \"major\",\n            \"title\": \"Turn-close recovery bypasses tool-result tier gate and can call the provider on over-large tool results\",\n            \"evidence\": \"The queued handler gates tool results with estimateTokens(content) > largeTierTokens and returns truncateForFallback(content) ready with no provider call in packages/lhc/src/domains/messages/internal/handlers.ts:145-159; intake even avoids queueing such work in packages/lhc/src/domains/messages/index.ts:150-196. The turn-close recovery path independently calls run.provider.summarizeToolResult with raw content at packages/lhc/src/domains/turns/internal/derive.ts:117-127, with no token check, no targetTokens, no paired tool name, and no guidance. That violates AC-2.3/AC-2.7 and the production-path invariant that large tool results truncate rather than inference-summarize.\",\n            \"affectedFiles\": [\n              \"packages/lhc/src/domains/turns/internal/derive.ts\",\n              \"packages/lhc/src/domains/messages/internal/handlers.ts\",\n              \"packages/lhc/src/domains/messages/index.ts\"\n            ],\n            \"requirementIds\": [\n              \"AC-2.3\",\n              \"AC-2.4\",\n              \"AC-2.7\",\n              \"AC-3.3\",\n              \"DD-3\"\n            ],\n            \"recommendedFixScope\": \"quick-fix\",\n            \"blocking\": true\n          }\n        ],\n        \"nonBlockingFindings\": [\n          {\n            \"id\": \"E06-NB-001\",\n            \"severity\": \"minor\",\n            \"title\": \"Form-to-derivation rename remains incomplete in production vocabulary\",\n            \"evidence\": \"The shared runtime type/schema moved to Derivation/derivation, but production files and exported/internal function names still use form vocabulary, including packages/lhc/src/domains/messages/internal/forms.ts, packages/lhc/src/domains/turns/internal/forms.ts, readMessageFormRows, readOwnedForms, and comments in packages/lhc/src/domains/turns/internal/compose.ts:172-186. This misses the epic scope statement that the codebase is renamed from form to derivation throughout.\",\n            \"affectedFiles\": [\n              \"packages/lhc/src/domains/messages/internal/forms.ts\",\n              \"packages/lhc/src/domains/turns/internal/forms.ts\",\n              \"packages/lhc/src/domains/turns/internal/compose.ts\",\n              \"packages/lhc/src/domains/messages/index.ts\"\n            ],\n            \"requirementIds\": [\n              \"Epic Scope: form-to-derivation rename\",\n              \"DD-1\"\n            ],\n            \"recommendedFixScope\": \"same-session-implementor\",\n            \"blocking\": false\n          }\n        ],\n        \"unresolvedItems\": [\n          \"Both gates passed, but the test run reported 9 skipped tests, including real-inference NOT-RAN because LHC_OPENROUTER_KEY was unset.\"\n        ],\n        \"gateResult\": \"pass\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"resultId\": \"07e552b8-e981-45e9-942f-3adf177d9d50\",\n        \"outcome\": \"block\",\n        \"provider\": \"codex\",\n        \"model\": \"gpt-5.5\",\n        \"reviewerLabel\": \"epic-reviewer-2\",\n        \"crossStoryFindings\": [\n          \"Story 3 fallback logging is not consistent with the Story 0 logging contract for every fallback event: absent derivation rows can render through a floor and record a gap without producing a log entry.\",\n          \"Story 0 rename is not complete across production source: multiple internal APIs and constants still use form terminology even though the epic retires form/Form naming in favor of derivation terminology.\"\n        ],\n        \"architectureFindings\": [\n          \"The main production execution path is real: createSdk requires exactly one explicit provider or inference config, compact reads stored material through the turns surface, and the Story/Epic gates pass.\",\n          \"Architecture drift remains in naming contracts: production modules still expose/read helpers named readMessageForms, readOwnedForms, readTurnFormRow, ComposeFormRow, composeFormKey, and MESSAGE_WORK_FORMS.\"\n        ],\n        \"epicCoverageAssessment\": [\n          \"AC coverage is broad and the package gate passes: pnpm run verify and pnpm run verify-all both completed successfully with 47 test files passed and 426 tests passed.\",\n          \"Coverage gap: turn fallback logging is tested for pending/failed rows, but not for absent derivation rows, which the production composer treats as fallback/gap cases.\",\n          \"Coverage gap: verify-all reported 9 skipped tests with NOT-RAN: real-inference (LHC_OPENROUTER_KEY unset).\"\n        ],\n        \"productionPathFindings\": [\n          \"No material fake adapters, hidden shims, placeholder providers, or non-real default execution paths were found in production assembly. The deterministic provider is explicit and not selected by createSdk as a default.\",\n          \"Smart compact does not call a provider in the inspected production path; it resolves chunk materials through turns.compactChunkMaterial and stored-member concatenation.\"\n        ],\n        \"blockingFindings\": [\n          {\n            \"id\": \"E06-BLOCK-001\",\n            \"severity\": \"major\",\n            \"title\": \"Absent derivation fallback is not logged\",\n            \"evidence\": \"packages/lhc/src/domains/turns/internal/compose.ts:222-238 creates a DependencyGap whenever a derivable component falls back, but creates a RecoveryReceipt only when form !== undefined. packages/lhc/src/domains/turns/internal/derive.ts:196-211 logs only recoveries, so an absent derivation row renders fallback content and records a gap without a fallback log entry. This violates AC-3.6's every-fallback logging contract.\",\n            \"affectedFiles\": [\n              \"packages/lhc/src/domains/turns/internal/compose.ts\",\n              \"packages/lhc/src/domains/turns/internal/derive.ts\"\n            ],\n            \"requirementIds\": [\n              \"AC-3.6\",\n              \"AC-5.3\"\n            ],\n            \"recommendedFixScope\": \"quick-fix\",\n            \"blocking\": true\n          }\n        ],\n        \"nonBlockingFindings\": [\n          {\n            \"id\": \"E06-NB-001\",\n            \"severity\": \"major\",\n            \"title\": \"Form terminology remains in production source after the rename epic\",\n            \"evidence\": \"The epic says form/Form naming is retired. Production source still contains form-named APIs and constants: ComposeFormRow/composeFormKey in packages/lhc/src/domains/turns/internal/compose.ts:38-49, MESSAGE_WORK_FORMS in packages/lhc/src/domains/messages/index.ts:135-140, readMessageForms/readMessageFormRow in packages/lhc/src/domains/messages/internal/forms.ts:74-120, readOwnedForms/readTurnFormRow in packages/lhc/src/domains/turns/internal/forms.ts:181-265, and imports/usages in packages/lhc/src/domains/turns/index.ts:33-35.\",\n            \"affectedFiles\": [\n              \"packages/lhc/src/domains/turns/internal/compose.ts\",\n              \"packages/lhc/src/domains/messages/index.ts\",\n              \"packages/lhc/src/domains/messages/internal/forms.ts\",\n              \"packages/lhc/src/domains/turns/internal/forms.ts\",\n              \"packages/lhc/src/domains/turns/index.ts\"\n            ],\n            \"requirementIds\": [\n              \"Story-0\",\n              \"DD-1\"\n            ],\n            \"recommendedFixScope\": \"fresh-fix-path\",\n            \"blocking\": false\n          },\n          {\n            \"id\": \"E06-NB-002\",\n            \"severity\": \"observation\",\n            \"title\": \"Real-inference tests did not run in the gate environment\",\n            \"evidence\": \"Both pnpm run verify and pnpm run verify-all exited 0, but the test output included NOT-RAN: real-inference (LHC_OPENROUTER_KEY unset) and reported 9 skipped tests.\",\n            \"affectedFiles\": [\n              \"packages/lhc/test/inference-real.test.ts\"\n            ],\n            \"requirementIds\": [\n              \"Gate Instructions\"\n            ],\n            \"recommendedFixScope\": \"human-ruling\",\n            \"blocking\": false\n          }\n        ],\n        \"unresolvedItems\": [\n          \"Need a rerun with real-inference credentials or an auth-independent real-inference gate path if this review must satisfy the local no-auth-skip testing preference.\"\n        ],\n        \"gateResult\": \"pass\"\n      }\n    ]\n  },\n  \"errors\": [],\n  \"warnings\": [],\n  \"artifacts\": [\n    {\n      \"kind\": \"result-envelope\",\n      \"path\": \"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/artifacts/epic/001-epic-review.json\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"startedAt\": \"2026-06-15T07:32:41.249Z\",\n  \"finishedAt\": \"2026-06-15T07:37:29.203Z\"\n}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
